    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors -\n    EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors()]{.doc-object-name\n    .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find every lowest common ancestor for many pairs of nodes in a DAG.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors()]{.doc-object-name\n    .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find every lowest common ancestor for many pairs of nodes in a DAG.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Find every lowest common ancestor for many pairs of nodes in a DAG.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind every lowest common ancestor for many pairs of nodes in a DAG.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L76769-L76897){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors(pairs=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![All-pairs all lowest common ancestors](../assets/graphs/all-pairs-all-lowest-common-ancestors.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Two parents, mum and dad, each with an edge down to both ann and bob, and eve standing alone. The queried nodes ann, bob and eve are outlined. For the pair ann, bob both parents are lowest common ancestors (accent color, with their four edges); ann and eve share no ancestor. The card maps (ann, bob) to mum and dad and keeps (ann, eve) with an empty list.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nApplies `all_lowest_common_ancestors()` to many pairs at once, sharing the ancestor\nsearches between pairs. Use it to find all the most specific shared categories of many\npairs of terms in an ontology with multiple inheritance, or every merge base of many\npairs of commits.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[pairs]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[tuple] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional list of `(u, v)` pairs (IDs or labels). If `None` (default), every pair of\n    nodes, including each node with itself.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[tuple[int, int], list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `(u, v)` to the IDs of its lowest common ancestors, in ID order, for every pair.\n    Unlike in `all_pairs_lowest_common_ancestor()`, a pair without a common ancestor is\n    kept, with an empty list.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is not a directed acyclic graph, is empty, or a node does not exist.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nEach node's ancestor set is computed once and cached; each pair then costs an\nintersection and a scan of the common ancestors' successors. This follows\n`all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors` from NetworkX pull request #7988.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~all_lowest_common_ancestors`) \n\n:   Every lowest common ancestor of one pair.\n\n[](`~all_pairs_lowest_common_ancestor`) \n\n:   One lowest common ancestor for each pair.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEvery pair is listed, with all its lowest common ancestors, and a pair with none gets\nan empty list:\n\n::: {#b5b2388d .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"D\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"D\"), (\"E\", \"F\")],\n    directed=True,\n)\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\nlca = graph.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors(\n    pairs=[(\"C\", \"D\"), (\"C\", \"F\")]\n)\n{\n    (label(u), label(v)): [label(w) for w in ws]\n    for (u, v), ws in lca.items()\n}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{('C', 'D'): ['A', 'B'], ('C', 'F'): []}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Meeting points of a program\n\n`courses()` holds the courses of a made-up computer science program, with an arrow from\neach course to every course that requires it. Of all the pairs of different courses,\nonly two have more than one lowest common ancestor:\n\n::: {#25aac20b .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ncourses = ec.courses()\nlabel = courses.get_label_from_id\nlca = courses.all_pairs_all_lowest_common_ancestors(\n    pairs=list(combinations(courses.get_node_ids(), 2))\n)\n\n[(label(u), label(v)) for (u, v), ws in lca.items() if len(ws) > 1]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[('CS350', 'CS460'), ('CS350', 'CS360')]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nCounting how often each course is a lowest common ancestor shows where the program's\npaths meet. Data Structures (CS102) is the meeting point of 45 pairs:\n\n::: {#13aa9501 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmeets = Counter(w for ws in lca.values() for w in ws)\ncourses.set_node_attrs(\"meets\", dict(meets))\n\n{label(n): k for n, k in meets.most_common(4)}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n{'CS102': 45, 'CS101': 11, 'MATH101': 6, 'MATH102': 5}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#50589a25 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nstages = dict(enumerate(courses.topological_generations()))\ncourses.layout_multipartite(subset_key=stages).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", size_by=\"meets\", color_by=\"dept\", label_by=\"label\",\n    height=420,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de